637:
It shall be unlawful for any minor to loiter, wander, stroll or play in or upon any public street, highway, road, lane, park, playground or other public ground, public place, public building, place of amusement, eating place, vacant lot or any place unsupervised by an adult having the lawful authority to be at such places between the hours of 11:00 p.m. on any day and 6:00 a.m. of the following day; provided, however, that on Fridays and Saturdays, the effective hours are between 12:00 midnight and 6:00 a.m. of the following day. The provisions of this section shall not apply in the following instances:
(1) When a minor is accompanied by his/her parent, guardian, or other adult person having lawful care and custody of the minor;
(2) When the minor is on an emergency errand for his/her parent or guardian or other adult person having the lawful care and custody of the minor;
(3) When the minor is returning directly home from a school or church activity;
(4) When the minor is returning directly home from lawful employment that makes it necessary to be in such places during the prescribed period of time;
(5) When the minor is attending or traveling directly to or from any activity involving the exercise of first amendment rights of freedom of speech, freedom of assembly, or free exercise of religion;
(6) When the minor is in a motor vehicle with parental consent for normal travel, with interstate travel through the city excepted in all cases from the curfew; and
(7) When the minor is on the property of or the sidewalk directly adjacent to the building in which he/she resides.
(Prior Code, § 39-2)

644:
(a) Public parks. It shall be unlawful to camp or to store personal property in any public park.
(b) Public streets. It shall be unlawful to camp, sleep, store personal property, sit, or lie down on any public street.
(c) Underneath bridges. It shall be unlawful to camp or store personal property underneath any bridge.
(d) Other property. It shall be unlawful to camp, sleep, store personal property, or to sit or lie down on any public property.
(e) Exceptions. This section shall not be construed to prohibit the following behavior:
